Rework SankofaApplyBootPatch onto the production updater interface (no shortcut):
- Patch path comes from a stored value (DartIsolate::SetSankofaBootPatchPath),
  set by the shell from sankofa_next_boot_patch_path() (the updater handles
  download / Ed25519-verify / version-select / rollback). Kept at runtime level
  so dart_isolate need not link libupdater — all updater C-API calls stay in the
  shell (correct engine layering).
- The manifest rides INSIDE the patch: the hook calls the module's embedded
  _sankofaManifest() -> List<String> and transplants each. The patch is ONE
  self-contained file the updater stages (no loose .names, no SANKOFA_PATCH_DIR).
- Vendored the updater C header (third_party/updater/include/updater_engine.h);
  libupdater.a already vendored for ios-arm64 + android arches.
Compile-verified (dart_isolate.o builds clean). Remaining shell wiring:
ConfigureSankofa (sankofa_init + next_boot_patch_path + report_launch_start +
SetSankofaBootPatchPath) + Shell report_launch_success + BUILD.gn libupdater link.

